 "limitations": [
  {
   "wanted": "A heat-set threaded insert (or the knob's own printed internal threads) as the load-bearing thread, instead of a captive hex nut",
   "blocked_by": "The hardware list only carries one insert, M3x4x5 (4.3 mm hole, M3 thread) - far too small for an M5 nut pocket; and the brief fixes the M5 ISO 4032 nut as the thread",
   "why": "An insert or printed threads would carry more torque and resist wear/creep better than a nut gripped in a printed hex, and would need no press-fit tuning"
  },
  {
   "wanted": "A true elastic snap - a thin split ring or three cantilever fingers inside the bore that the nut pops past, so retention is positive (a lip behind the nut) rather than friction",
   "blocked_by": "Only stiff, fatigue-prone PLA on a 0.4 mm nozzle, and the brief's \"presses in by hand\" + \"no glue\": a 0.1 mm/side snap in thick-walled PLA needs a crushing force (my estimate: several hundred newtons) and would split the knob, so I fell back to a light interference fit plus a hard mechanical stop",
   "why": "It would make fall-out impossible even if the print comes out loose, instead of relying on the pocket being a few hundredths undersized"
  }
 ],
